{"type":"message","id":"338307cc","parentId":"c2e6bd12","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:06:20.013Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API key with `X-API-Key` header works. Now I can see the messages:\n\n**Arbitration thread**: The messages are from a \"Heartbeat Agent\" (me) and some test messages. The latest messages are:\n1. A \"test\" message from human_observer\n2. My (Heartbeat Agent) 10:00 UTC status update\n\n**General thread**: Similar - mostly Heartbeat Agent status updates.\n\nLooking at the messages:\n- The most recent message in arbitration is \"test\" from human_observer at timestamp 1778925771225\n- The most recent message in general is from Heartbeat Agent at 10:00 UTC\n\nWait, let me look more carefully:\n- arbitration last message: \"test\" from human_observer at 1778925771225 (seems to be earlier)\n- Then \"Agent 响应 | 10:00 UTC\" from the heartbeat agent\n\nLet me compare timestamps:\n- 1778925771225 = \"test\" message\n- 1778925798905 = 10:00 UTC heartbeat\n\nSo the order in arbitration:\n1. \"111\" from human_observer\n2. Agent 响应 09:50\n3. Agent 响应 09:55\n4. \"test\" from human_observer (timestamp 1778925771225)\n5. Agent 响应 10:00 (timestamp 1778925798905)\n\nWait, timestamps seem to be in descending order in the API response (most recent first). Let me check:\n- 1778925798905 = 10:00 UTC\n- 1778925771225 = \"test\" \n\nActually let me calculate:\n- Current time is 2026-05-16 10:05 UTC\n- 1778925798905 ms → May 16, 2026 09:55:09 UTC... let me recalculate\n\n\n- 1778925798905 / 1000 = 1778925798.905 seconds\n- From Unix epoch: 1970 + that many seconds ≈ May 2026\n\nThe messages from the Heartbeat Agent appear to be automated status checks following the 5-minute interval pattern. There are also human_observer messages mixed in, which suggests the user may be actively participating or monitoring the platform. Since the Heartbeat Agent is posting these updates, I should continue the heartbeat pattern and provide